@model Reflect.ProviderDashboard.Web.Models.ViewModels.Provider.Trust.TrustViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Trust and connectivity";
}
<div class="mb-4">
    <p class="eyebrow">Company handoff</p>
    <h1 class="page-title mb-1">Trust and connectivity</h1>
    <p class="text-muted fs-13 mb-0">Time stored in UTC for RDS PostgreSQL. Displayed in the company zone. Synthetic records only — HIPAA-aligned target, not a certified production system.</p>
</div>

<section class="work-panel" aria-labelledby="arch-heading">
    <h2 id="arch-heading">Architecture</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">Future production path. This prototype implements the dashboard, UTC clock, TLS, and a signed ingest hook.</p>
    <ol class="arch-flow">
        <li>
            <strong>Reflect XR / Mobile</strong>
            <span>Session events leave the headset or app over TLS.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Ingest options</strong>
            <span>HTTPS JSON API, nightly encrypted batch, or future FHIR from the EHR.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Clinical API</strong>
            <span>Auth, audit, minimum-necessary access. HIPAA boundary.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL</strong>
            <span><code>timestamptz</code> in UTC. Encrypted at rest. Company BAA.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Provider dashboard</strong>
            <span>Converts UTC to @Model.TimeZoneLabel (@Model.TimeZoneIana) for clinicians. HTTPS + HSTS.</span>
        </li>
    </ol>
</section>

<section class="work-panel" aria-labelledby="tz-heading">
    <h2 id="tz-heading">Time zones</h2>
    <p>Every session, assignment, and comparison window is stored as UTC. The dashboard never writes a local wall-clock to the database. Display uses the company zone so a facility in one region does not mix offsets.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Storage contract: RDS PostgreSQL <code>timestamptz</code>, UTC.</li>
        <li>Display zone: <strong>@Model.TimeZoneLabel</strong> · <code>@Model.TimeZoneIana</code> (configurable in <code>Company:TimeZone</code>).</li>
        <li>Source details still show the original UTC instant.</li>
        <li>Needs Attention windows are computed in UTC, then labeled in @Model.TimeZoneLabel.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="work-panel" aria-labelledby="ingest-heading">
    <h2 id="ingest-heading">How data can be uploaded</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">Three company options. The first is wired in this prototype behind an integration key.</p>
    <article class="signal-card">
        <h3>1. HTTPS JSON ingest (ready now)</h3>
        <p><code>POST @Model.IngestPath</code> with header <code>X-Reflect-Integration-Key</code>. Send <code>startedAt</code> with an offset or <code>Z</code>; the server stores UTC. Integration is @(Model.IntegrationEnabled ? "enabled in this environment" : "disabled until Integration:Enabled is set").</p>
        <pre class="ingest-sample" tabindex="0">POST /api/v1/ingest/sessions
X-Reflect-Integration-Key: (facility secret)
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalPatientId": "PT-10085",
  "startedAt": "2026-11-06T16:00:00-05:00",
  "durationMinutes": 24,
  "platform": "Mobile",
  "moduleName": "Mood Check-in",
  "reflectionSummary": "Synthetic ingest example",
  "affectScore": 6,
  "hardwareId": "MOB-7740"
}</pre>
    </article>
    <article class="signal-card">
        <h3>2. Encrypted batch (future nightly load)</h3>
        <p>CSV or Parquet dropped to a private S3 bucket (KMS) or SFTP. A worker normalizes timestamps to UTC and upserts into RDS. Use when XR/Mobile cannot call the API in real time.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="signal-card">
        <h3>3. EHR / FHIR R4 (future)</h3>
        <p>Encounter and Observation resources from the facility EHR over mutually authenticated TLS. Map patient MRN to <code>externalPatientId</code>. Same UTC storage rule.</p>
    </article>
    <p>Private connectivity later: VPC peering or PrivateLink from Reflect XR into the clinical API. No public database ports.</p>
</section>

<section class="work-panel" aria-labelledby="hipaa-heading">
    <h2 id="hipaa-heading">HIPAA check</h2>
    <p><strong>This demo is not a HIPAA-covered production system.</strong> Records are fictional. The production target is HIPAA-aligned:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Business Associate Agreement with the cloud provider (for example AWS RDS).</li>
        <li>Unique clinician IDs, unique user authentication, automatic logoff (1-hour cookie here), emergency access procedure owned by the facility.</li>
        <li>Encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest (RDS encryption + KMS).</li>
        <li>Audit controls on access to electronic PHI; this prototype logs HTTP but does not yet retain a clinical audit table.</li>
        <li>Minimum necessary: a provider sees only assigned patients.</li>
        <li>Integrity: hashed passwords, antiforgery on browser posts, UTC timestamps that cannot drift by local clock.</li>
        <li>Transmission security: HTTPS redirection, HSTS in Production, CSP, no PHI in query strings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-muted">A covered entity still needs workforce training, facility policies, and a risk analysis. Those are organizational, not this prototype.</p>
</section>

<section class="work-panel" aria-labelledby="cia-heading">
    <h2 id="cia-heading">Security (CIA)</h2>
    <table class="table">
        <caption>Confidentiality, integrity, availability in this system</caption>
        <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">Goal</th>
            <th scope="col">How it is met</th>
        </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">Confidentiality</th>
            <td>TLS certificate on the connection@(Model.HttpsActive ? " (this request is HTTPS)" : " (this request is HTTP — use the HTTPS URL)"), role-based sign-in, assignment-scoped caseload, CSP, no-store cache headers, HttpOnly cookies.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">Integrity</th>
            <td>ASP.NET Identity password hashes, antiforgery tokens on forms, fixed-time API key compare on ingest, UTC storage so session order cannot shift with a local timezone.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">Availability</th>
            <td>Rate limits on account and ingest, liveness at <code>/health/live</code>, HSTS@(Model.HstsEnabled ? " on" : " reserved for Production") so browsers keep using HTTPS.</td>
        </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>

<section class="work-panel" aria-labelledby="cert-heading">
    <h2 id="cert-heading">Secure certificate</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Local: ASP.NET Core HTTPS development certificate on <code>https://localhost:7150</code>.</li>
        <li>Hosted demo: the platform’s managed certificate (Render / Azure / ACM on a load balancer).</li>
        <li>Production: AWS Certificate Manager or Azure managed TLS 1.2+, HTTP redirected to HTTPS, HSTS max-age at least one year.</li>
        <li>This session: <strong>@(Model.HttpsActive ? "HTTPS is active" : "HTTPS is not active")</strong>. HSTS: <strong>@(Model.HstsEnabled ? "enabled" : "off in Development")</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
</section>
